<title>MEXICO: Mexico set to auction Cancun port project - report.</title>
<headline>Mexico set to auction Cancun port project - report.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico is set to auction the rights to build a major new port in the Caribbean tourist resort of Cancun, state-owned news agency Notimex said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The project could be worth up to $500 million, Notimex quoted Emilio Gamboa Patron, the head of the state-run tourism development agency Fonatur, as saying.</p>
<p>Patron said the project would take five years and would allow Cancun to receive the world's top cruise ships, according to Notimex.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
